  - [Crow] Goodnight, punk.

734
00:28:56,134 --> 00:28:58,101
  - The queen wouldn't
  deny her sister anything.

735
00:28:58,101 --> 00:29:00,268
 - [Billis] I know, and
 I'm here to ask her

736
00:29:00,268 --> 00:29:02,901
  for the greatest
  favor of my life.

737
00:29:02,901 --> 00:29:04,301
 - Everyone in court
 knows the only favor

738
00:29:04,301 --> 00:29:05,968
 that will satisfy
 the Princess Billis.

739
00:29:05,968 --> 00:29:08,034
 - [Joel] Guys, I am
 so homesick right now.

740
00:29:08,034 --> 00:29:11,334
 - What is it?
 - I must talk to you, Samara.

741
00:29:11,334 --> 00:29:12,534
 - [Samara] Get out.

742
00:29:12,534 --> 00:29:14,401
 - [Crow] Okay, I'll
 come back later.

743
00:29:14,401 --> 00:29:15,668
 - [Joel] Hey, it's
 a Flintstone phone.

744
00:29:15,668 --> 00:29:18,568
- I want you to promise
that you'll hear me out.

745
00:29:18,568 --> 00:29:21,268
  - [Tom] I'll hear you out
  that door is what I'll do.

746
00:29:21,268 --> 00:29:23,068
 - Haven't I always done so?

747
00:29:23,068 --> 00:29:25,068
 - [Joel] Marlo
 Thomas is That Queen,

748
00:29:25,068 --> 00:29:27,101
- Don't you really
believe I'm fond of you?

749
00:29:27,101 --> 00:29:28,734
 - Oh don't say that, Samara.

750
00:29:28,734 --> 00:29:31,034
 Even if we didn't
 have the same mother,

751
00:29:31,034 --> 00:29:33,601
 you've always been a
 perfect sister to me.

752
00:29:33,601 --> 00:29:35,268
 - [Crow] Rip!

753
00:29:35,268 --> 00:29:37,868
 - I want it to be perfectly
 clear that my attitude

754
00:29:37,868 --> 00:29:40,301
 is dictated solely by
 my affection for you.

755
00:29:40,301 --> 00:29:41,901
 - Of course.

756
00:29:41,901 --> 00:29:43,468
 And because of that
 affection, you could make me

757
00:29:43,468 --> 00:29:45,701
the happiest woman in the world.

758
00:29:45,701 --> 00:29:48,101
  Samara, Prince Darix loves
  me, and if you'll only

759
00:29:48,101 --> 00:29:50,968
give your consent, we'll
be married immediately.

760
00:29:50,968 --> 00:29:52,268
 - [Tom] Looks like this
 movie's equipped with airbags.

761
00:29:52,268 --> 00:29:55,334
 - [Joel] Ooh...
 - [Tom] Sorry, sorry.

762
00:29:55,334 --> 00:29:56,868
- Of course not.

763
00:29:56,868 --> 00:29:58,634
How could I refuse you?

764
00:29:58,634 --> 00:30:00,968
 - [Crow] No, no, no, no, no!

765
00:30:03,834 --> 00:30:07,634
 - Oh Samara, why are
 you making us wait?

766
00:30:07,634 --> 00:30:09,634
- It's been my intention
for a long time now

767
00:30:09,634 --> 00:30:11,734
 to send Prince Darix
 to the court of Corum

768
00:30:11,734 --> 00:30:12,968
to conduct secret negotiations.

769
00:30:12,968 --> 00:30:14,601
 - [Tom] Uh, back in
 the frame, please.

770
00:30:14,601 --> 00:30:16,801
 - Matters of
 greatest delicacy...

771
00:30:16,801 --> 00:30:18,268
 - [Joel] Toilet paper.

772
00:30:18,268 --> 00:30:21,301
- But he'll be back soon and
you'll live happily ever after.

773
00:30:21,301 --> 00:30:22,634
  - [Crow] The end.

774
00:30:22,634 --> 00:30:23,868
  - Thank you, dear sister.

775
00:30:23,868 --> 00:30:25,134
  - [Tom] Um, leave
  the ring please.

776
00:30:25,134 --> 00:30:26,801
- He'll be leaving first
thing tomorrow morning.

777
00:30:26,801 --> 00:30:29,234
 While he'll be away from you,
 it won't be for very long.

778
00:30:29,234 --> 00:30:30,534
 - [Crow] Do-si-do
 with an evil queen.

779
00:30:30,534 --> 00:30:32,834
 (humming square dance music)

780
00:30:32,834 --> 00:30:34,668
 - [Joel] Not for long.

781
00:30:36,568 --> 00:30:39,301
  - Claudius is dead,
  Hercules has disappeared.

782
00:30:39,301 --> 00:30:40,601
 - [Tom] And I'm outta here.

783
00:30:40,601 --> 00:30:42,034
 - The two of them were
 the only hope we had.

784
00:30:42,034 --> 00:30:43,468
 There's nothing left to do.

785
00:30:43,468 --> 00:30:46,034
- You can talk that way because
you don't have children,

786
00:30:46,034 --> 00:30:47,934
but if you had a
daughter like my child,

787
00:30:47,934 --> 00:30:50,601
 you'd understand the
 anguish that a mother feels

788
00:30:50,601 --> 00:30:52,101
  when the moon is
  full and you know

789
00:30:52,101 --> 00:30:53,934
  they're coming to take
  her away to be sacrificed.

790
00:30:53,934 --> 00:30:54,901
 - [Joel] It's Lee Meriwether.

791
00:30:54,901 --> 00:30:56,068
  (applause)

792
00:30:56,068 --> 00:30:56,968
 - My wife is right.

793
00:30:56,968 --> 00:30:59,701
- [Crow] Mickey Rourke!

794
00:30:59,701 --> 00:31:01,234
- You're the only one
who's been to the top of

795
00:31:01,234 --> 00:31:03,601
the Mountain of Death, tell
them what happened to you there.

796
00:31:03,601 --> 00:31:05,401
 Speak out, tell us
 whether ordinary men

797
00:31:05,401 --> 00:31:07,068
  can overcome the monsters.

798
00:31:07,068 --> 00:31:08,868
 - I saw the mountain
 open up miraculously

799
00:31:08,868 --> 00:31:10,968
 and I was bathed in a
 blinding green light.

800
00:31:10,968 --> 00:31:12,401
 - [Tom] It was great.

801
00:31:12,401 --> 00:31:14,534
 - Then huge, deformed
 rock-like Moon Mans appeared

802
00:31:14,534 --> 00:31:16,601
  and at the same time I was
  deafened by a weird sound

803
00:31:16,601 --> 00:31:18,801
that seemed to come from
the depths of the Earth.

804
00:31:18,801 --> 00:31:20,401
 After that, I don't
 remember anything.

805
00:31:20,401 --> 00:31:21,668
 I was so terrified--

806
00:31:21,668 --> 00:31:23,168
 - [Crow] I wet 'em.

807
00:31:23,168 --> 00:31:25,801
  - I came to after a while
  and I found I was alone.

808
00:31:25,801 --> 00:31:27,234
 - Your experience
 only confirms the fact

809
00:31:27,234 --> 00:31:29,334
 that it will not be
 easy for us to win.

810
00:31:29,334 --> 00:31:30,634
- T think it's useless.
- [Tom] Harvey Korman!

811
00:31:30,634 --> 00:31:33,068
 (applauding)

812
00:31:34,234 --> 00:31:35,334
- All I can say is this.

813
00:31:35,334 --> 00:31:37,201
 (blubbering)

814
00:31:37,201 --> 00:31:40,968
 - [Tom] Roddy MacDowell, yay!
 (applauding)

815
00:31:40,968 --> 00:31:42,601
 - I swear to you that
 I am not influenced

816
00:31:42,601 --> 00:31:44,234
  by any personal ambition.

817
00:31:44,234 --> 00:31:46,201
 The only thing I want
 is to liberate Samar

818
00:31:46,201 --> 00:31:47,901
 from the nightmare
 that's afflicting us.

819
00:31:47,901 --> 00:31:49,168
- [Joel] And to direct.

820
00:31:49,168 --> 00:31:50,901
  - Then my wife and
  I will go away,

821
00:31:50,901 --> 00:31:53,634
  asking nothing,
  accepting nothing.

822
00:31:53,634 --> 00:31:54,901
 - [Crow] Lee Majors,
 ladies and gentlemen!

823
00:31:54,901 --> 00:31:56,434
  (applause)

824
00:31:56,434 --> 00:31:58,368
  - My name is Timor, and
  it's on the list of those

825
00:31:58,368 --> 00:32:00,501
 who have been selected as the
 victims for the sacrifice.

826
00:32:00,501 --> 00:32:01,734
 - [Tom] Yeah, boo-hoo.

827
00:32:01,734 --> 00:32:03,201
but I prefer to die in
combat with the monsters

828
00:32:03,201 --> 00:32:04,901
 if my death will help
 to liberate Samar.

829
00:32:04,901 --> 00:32:07,334
 - [Joel] Robert Stack.
 (applause)

830
00:32:07,334 --> 00:32:10,034
  - Quiet, don't
  let them hear you.

831
00:32:10,034 --> 00:32:11,368
 - [Tom] Ixnay, shh.

832
00:32:11,368 --> 00:32:12,434
  We weren't doing nothing.

833
00:32:12,434 --> 00:32:15,368
It's Clavius, he started it all.

834
00:32:15,368 --> 00:32:19,168
 - [Crow] Paul Sorvino!
 (applause)

835
00:32:19,168 --> 00:32:20,134
- [Agar] It is I, Agar,

836
00:32:20,134 --> 00:32:23,234
with a friend.
- [Joel] Agarn?

837
00:32:23,234 --> 00:32:24,634
 - [Tom] Marlo Thomas,
 ladies and gentlemen!

838
00:32:24,634 --> 00:32:27,301
 Marlo Thomas!
 (applause)

839
00:32:27,301 --> 00:32:29,501
 - Welcome, Hercules!

840
00:32:29,501 --> 00:32:31,901
 - [Joel] Oh, it's Herc
 and he's got the keg!

841
00:32:31,901 --> 00:32:33,868
  (cracking)

842
00:32:33,868 --> 00:32:35,634
  - With you leading
  us, we will win.

843
00:32:35,634 --> 00:32:37,101
 - Let me present Prince Darix.

844
00:32:37,101 --> 00:32:39,268
  - [Tom] Prince Darix, yay.

845
00:32:40,234 --> 00:32:42,901
- We'll get along well together.

846
00:32:44,168 --> 00:32:45,601
  - [Joel] Uh, Herc,
  you got hat hair.

847
00:32:45,601 --> 00:32:47,934
 - I know of the tragic
 destiny that hangs over you

848
00:32:47,934 --> 00:32:50,734
 but what would happen if
 one day, the people of Samar

849
00:32:50,734 --> 00:32:53,468
were to refuse to send
the sacrificial victims

850
00:32:53,468 --> 00:32:55,001
to the monsters of the mountain?

851
00:32:55,001 --> 00:32:56,168
  - [Crow] I think it would
  go something like this.

852
00:32:56,168 --> 00:32:58,768
 (theme music)

853
00:33:01,768 --> 00:33:03,034
 - I never thought
 the time would come

854
00:33:03,034 --> 00:33:04,568
  when I would great
  you with such joy

855
00:33:04,568 --> 00:33:07,368
 and in the same breath
 have to say goodbye.

856
00:33:07,368 --> 00:33:08,701
  - Watch and you'll
  see that my horse

857
00:33:08,701 --> 00:33:11,401
  will fly on the
  wind like Pegasus.

858
00:33:11,401 --> 00:33:14,334
- Take care of yourself,
and come back soon.

859
00:33:14,334 --> 00:33:15,701
  When can I hope
  to see you again?

860
00:33:15,701 --> 00:33:16,934
- In a few days.
- [Crow] Soon?

861
00:33:16,934 --> 00:33:18,701
 - You've spoken of
 it to Queen Samara?

862
00:33:18,701 --> 00:33:20,534
  - Yes, when she was
  giving me the instructions

863
00:33:20,534 --> 00:33:22,668
 for the mission I'm to
 carry out for her in Corum,

864
00:33:22,668 --> 00:33:25,101
 she made several references
 to our marriage plans.

865
00:33:25,101 --> 00:33:26,701
  - [Tom] Stayczek,
  you gettin' this?

866
00:33:26,701 --> 00:33:27,634
- By the way your sister spoke,

867
00:33:27,634 --> 00:33:29,268
it seems she has no objections.

868
00:33:29,268 --> 00:33:31,234
 They're sending me
 off as her ambassador,

869
00:33:31,234 --> 00:33:32,668
 in such good faith.

870
00:33:32,668 --> 00:33:34,601
- Well now you're the most
important relative of the Queen.

871
00:33:34,601 --> 00:33:38,001
 - [Joel] Oh ho ho,
 you really think so?

872
00:33:38,001 --> 00:33:40,134
  - [All] Kiss her, come on!

873
00:33:40,134 --> 00:33:41,068
- [Crow] Why don't you kiss her

874
00:33:41,068 --> 00:33:43,868
instead of talking her to death?

875
00:33:43,868 --> 00:33:45,834
- [Tom] Could you have
a platonic relationship
before Plato?

876
00:33:45,834 --> 00:33:47,001
 - [Joel] Hmmm.

877
00:33:49,034 --> 00:33:50,234
 Ah, she's all gassed up, sir.

878
00:33:50,234 --> 00:33:52,401
  I vacuumed the inside too.

879
00:33:54,401 --> 00:33:55,368
  - [Tom] Those are
  tegular saddles

880
00:33:55,368 --> 00:33:57,868
with blankets thrown over them!

881
00:33:57,868 --> 00:34:01,034
 - [Crow] Have fun
 stormin' the castle!

882
00:34:07,068 --> 00:34:08,568
- Is is true that Darix
has been sent away

883
00:34:08,568 --> 00:34:09,634
  on orders from the queen?

884
00:34:09,634 --> 00:34:12,468
- Yes.
- [Joel] Slumber party!

885
00:34:12,468 --> 00:34:13,468
 - What are you trying to say?

886
00:34:13,468 --> 00:34:14,734
 - [Crow] He's toast.

887
00:34:14,734 --> 00:34:15,901
  - I don't want to
  alarm you, Billis,

888
00:34:15,901 --> 00:34:17,501
 but I think it's
 necessary you be told.

889
00:34:17,501 --> 00:34:18,634
The queen's aware that Darix is

890
00:34:18,634 --> 00:34:20,168
 taking part in the conspiracy.

891
00:34:20,168 --> 00:34:21,568
- But you think he's in danger>

892
00:34:21,568 --> 00:34:23,068
 - Yes, I think he's
 walking into a trap.

893
00:34:23,068 --> 00:34:23,901
  - Oh Agar.

894
00:34:25,401 --> 00:34:27,901
  - Come with me, I know a
  man who's powerful enough

895
00:34:27,901 --> 00:34:30,168
  to help us both, and I'm
  sure he won't refuse you.

896
00:34:30,168 --> 00:34:31,101
- [Joel] He's really reasonable

897
00:34:31,101 --> 00:34:34,434
and won't charge for the extras.

898
00:34:34,434 --> 00:34:37,834
- [Tom] Herc's playing
cartoon tag over there.

899
00:34:37,834 --> 00:34:40,101
 - [Crow] They're devolving.

900
00:34:42,534 --> 00:34:43,834
- [Tom] Isn't he worried
dirt's gonna stick

901
00:34:43,834 --> 00:34:46,501
to all that oil he's got on him?

902
00:34:47,968 --> 00:34:50,568
 - Along that road, they take
 the victims to the sacrifice.

903
00:34:50,568 --> 00:34:53,001
 Beyond those woods and the
 rivers, the Mountain of Death.

904
00:34:53,001 --> 00:34:55,901
 - [Tom] Let's buy a pass so
 we can go on all the rides.

905
00:34:55,901 --> 00:34:57,401
  - [Agar] Hercules!

906
00:34:57,401 --> 00:35:00,268
 - [Joel] I thought you were
 out of town this weekend!

907
00:35:00,268 --> 00:35:02,034
  - [Tom] Zeus is on line
  three, you wanna take it?

908
00:35:02,034 --> 00:35:03,834
 - They told us at the
 tavern you'd be here.

909
00:35:03,834 --> 00:35:05,668
 The Princess Billis
 needs your help.

910
00:35:05,668 --> 00:35:07,168
  - At your service.

911
00:35:07,168 --> 00:35:09,201
 - The queen has sent Darix
 away on a mission to Corum.

912
00:35:09,201 --> 00:35:11,034
- It's only a pretext,
she found out that Darix

913
00:35:11,034 --> 00:35:12,701
 is one of the conspirators.

914
00:35:12,701 --> 00:35:14,101
 - Timor, get my horse, fast.

915
00:35:14,101 --> 00:35:15,301
 - [Crow] Get my fast horse.

916
00:35:15,301 --> 00:35:16,501
 - Darix is already
 on the road to Corum?

917
00:35:16,501 --> 00:35:18,434
  - Yes, he left
  about an hour ago.

918
00:35:18,434 --> 00:35:20,268
 - [Joel] Well, oh hi.

919
00:35:20,268 --> 00:35:22,534
- You had better go back
to the palace, Princess.

920
00:35:22,534 --> 00:35:24,201
 And don't be afraid.

921
00:35:26,901 --> 00:35:29,968
  Even if it costs me my
  life, Darix will be saved.

922
00:35:29,968 --> 00:35:31,201
 - [Agar] Hercules--

923
00:35:31,201 --> 00:35:35,434
- [Tom] Please don't go
to any trouble for us.

924
00:35:35,434 --> 00:35:37,601
  - [Joel] I give
  'em three months.

925
00:35:37,601 --> 00:35:38,834
 - [Crow] Herc, would
 you help us move?

926
00:35:38,834 --> 00:35:40,934
  - [Tom] Even if
  it costs my life.

927
00:35:40,934 --> 00:35:43,068
  - I trust you to get them
  safely back to the city.

928
00:35:43,068 --> 00:35:46,134
  - [Tom] Even if it
  costs you my life.

929
00:35:47,634 --> 00:35:49,901
 - [Joel] Yeah, now Herc'll
 go to a bar for a few hours

930
00:35:49,901 --> 00:35:51,268
 and say he couldn't find him.

931
00:35:51,268 --> 00:35:53,601
 (chuckling)

932
00:35:56,301 --> 00:36:00,401
♪ She was calling Wildfire, wild

933
00:36:02,101 --> 00:36:05,868
  - [Tom] Ow, ow, ow,
  owie, owie, ow, ow, ouch.

934
00:36:09,134 --> 00:36:12,168
 - [Crow] Ah, then
 Prokofiev showed up!

935
00:36:12,168 --> 00:36:13,668
  - [Tom] Hey, whoa!

936
00:36:16,234 --> 00:36:18,434
 Sergei, keep it down will ya?

937
00:36:18,434 --> 00:36:19,268
Jiminy.

938
00:36:25,968 --> 00:36:30,134
 - [Joel] Hey, there's a lot of
 them little guys down there.

939
00:36:32,601 --> 00:36:36,968
 - [Joel] Thundering hoofbeats
 and a mighty hi-ho Silver.

940
00:36:36,968 --> 00:36:38,868
- [Crow] Not the cliff!

941
00:36:41,901 --> 00:36:45,501
  (humming trumpet fanfares)

942
00:36:49,768 --> 00:36:52,401
♪ Hey, it's the Undersea Kingdom

943
00:36:52,401 --> 00:36:57,068
 ♪ For you and me and it's fun

944
00:36:57,068 --> 00:36:58,401
 - [Tom] Whoa, an apple tree!

945
00:36:58,401 --> 00:37:00,534
  (yelling)

946
00:37:00,534 --> 00:37:01,334
 Oh hi.

947
00:37:06,501 --> 00:37:10,034
 - [Crow] Lawrence of Arabia.
 - [Tom] Lawrence.

948
00:37:10,034 --> 00:37:11,201
  Would you call
  this a light trot?

949
00:37:11,201 --> 00:37:12,701
- [Joel] No, it's
really more of a canter

950
00:37:12,701 --> 00:37:14,334
but not quite a gallop.

951
00:37:14,334 --> 00:37:17,168
  - [Tom] Trot-ish,
  though, I think.

952
00:37:22,301 --> 00:37:23,768
 Whoa, whoa.

953
00:37:23,768 --> 00:37:25,701
  You should get four-wheel
  drive next time, Tom.

954
00:37:25,701 --> 00:37:28,034
 - What are you doing?

955
00:37:28,034 --> 00:37:29,001
 Ah!

956
00:37:29,001 --> 00:37:31,434
 - [Joel] Oh, I see, got it.

957
00:37:31,434 --> 00:37:35,168
  - [Tom] Now it's an
  Arrow shirt he's wearing.

958
00:37:36,168 --> 00:37:39,234
 - [Crow] Just a flesh wound.

959
00:37:39,234 --> 00:37:42,368
  - [Tom] Bet that
  horse has no name.

960
00:37:42,368 --> 00:37:45,534
 - [Joel] Hey, come
 back with my arrow!

961
00:37:47,568 --> 00:37:51,301
 ♪ Marvel the mustang,
 he's almost for real

962
00:37:51,301 --> 00:37:55,468
 ♪ This one's from Hercules,
 this one's from Hercules

963
00:38:01,634 --> 00:38:04,201
- [Crow] Just drop me anywhere.

964
00:38:09,068 --> 00:38:11,801
  - [Joel] I'm a
  Grimwauld warrior!

965
00:38:12,734 --> 00:38:15,401
- [All] Pizza pizza pizza pizza

966
00:38:15,401 --> 00:38:18,901
 - [Joel] Stop hurting
 him, he's my friend!

967
00:38:20,901 --> 00:38:23,001
